<!--
	HEAT -- sweat and a flush, DURING a scene rather than after it.

	The only sets here whose textures Rapport ships. Every other set on this page
	drives CumOverlays' assets; these had nothing to drive. Measured across all 16
	overlay packs installed on the development machine: 959 templates, of which 925
	paint biped slot 3, 34 paint slot 4, and NONE paints the head or matches sweat
	or blush by any spelling. AAF cannot make up the difference either -- its
	overlay vocabulary is template/alpha/isFemale (common.xsd, overlayType), so it
	applies a texture at an opacity and cannot tint one. See tools/make_overlays.py.

	TWO GROUPS, not one group of two. `quantity` PICKS from a group, so a single
	group holding both templates would apply one of them at random -- sweat or
	blush, never both. A group of one each is what makes both certain.

	The body and the face are separate biped slots (3 and 0), which is why one set
	can carry both without either fighting the other.

	No duration, for the same reason as every set above: AAF's removal timer is an
	in-session one that a save, a reload or a crash mid-count all lose, and an
	overlay stranded that way never comes off. Rapport owns removal instead --
	Expressions::CollectClear, off the same _wearing list that guarantees a face
	comes off, which is persisted into the save.

	SLOT 0 DOES NOT WORK -- MEASURED, not assumed. Three blush templates on biped
	slot 0 were shipped and watched in game across several scenes: the faces were
	unchanged. F4EE does not apply a head overlay. That is consistent with the
	census (not one of the 959 installed templates targets the head) and it is why
	there is no blush here any more. A flush needs the CharGen tint layer or worn
	geometry, not an overlay. Do not re-add a slot-0 template expecting it to draw.
-->

<overlaySet id="Rapport_Heat_1">
	<condition isFemale="true">
		<overlayGroup quantity="1">
			<overlay template="Rapport_Sweat_1" alpha="100" isFemale="true"/>
		</overlayGroup>
	</condition>
	<condition isFemale="false">
		<overlayGroup quantity="1">
			<overlay template="Rapport_Sweat_1" alpha="100" isFemale="false"/>
		</overlayGroup>
	</condition>
</overlaySet>

